# Z-SPAN top-level gitignore.
# (The Navigator subdir at 02_Core_Project/council_navigator/
#  has its own .gitignore with frontend/Python-specific rules.)

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Cloudflare wrangler CLI artifacts (build cache, deploy assets state).
# Created when the operator runs `wrangler pages deploy` from repo root
# (session-87 emergency-recovery flow after CF Pages auto-build shipped
# a mismatched hash on b118f90). Local tooling state; never committed.
.wrangler/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
venv/
venv_*/
.venv/
.venv-worker/
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.backup

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.local
*.local
# Mac transcriber node bearer token — never commit
**/.bearer_token

# OAuth / service-account credential downloads (Google Cloud).
# Default download names from console.cloud.google.com → Credentials.
# These authorize writes to YouTube (Proofs uploads, T-009 Phase 2) and
# other on-behalf-of-user operations — NEVER commit.
# Credential home directory — gitignored as a WHOLE DIRECTORY so safety
# doesn't depend on exact filename patterns (D-104 audit F-1; relocated
# from repo root 2026-06-13). The filename patterns above/below stay as
# belt-and-braces for legacy root-level downloads.
**/secrets/
client_secret*.json
*_oauth*.json
*.credentials.json
service-account*.json
# YouTube refresh token, persisted after the one-time OAuth consent flow.
youtube_refresh_token.json

# Voiceprint embeddings — PAUSED + untracked 2026-07-01 (Fable-5 audit F5).
# Biometric-adjacent data of named individuals must not ride the repo that
# Prong D flips public. Files stay on disk (local use is operator-accepted
# for now); git history still contains the 5 pre-pause files — the
# pre-public-flip history-remake gate row in LAUNCH_GATES covers that.
**/city_intelligence/*/voices/

# Runtime data / artifacts (regenerable, large, or sensitive)
**/meetings_cache.db
**/meetings_cache.db-shm
**/meetings_cache.db-wal
# Prod-DB forensic archives — contain operator PII in published_by rows.
# NEVER track; repo is public-bound. (session-88 CF audit HIGH-3)
ops/prod_db_archive/
# Additional PII-bearing files flagged by the session-89 three-way security
# audit (sol MEDIUM): local username/path/LAN endpoint + owner email. Seal
# against a stray git add before the fresh-repo public flip.
02_Core_Project/pc_agent_relay/STATUS.json
ops/REMAKE2_EXECUTION_NOTES.md
**/user_settings.json
**/orchestrator_autonomy.json
**/parser_test_results.json
**/FINAL_HEALTH_REPORT.json

# NotebookLM Studio media (regenerable, multi-MB / multi-GB)
**/media/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Node
node_modules/
/operator_only/
dist/
.pnpm-store/

# Built distribution artifacts — never tracked (sol Finding #2, 2026-07-25).
# The tracked `zspan_cli-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl` was built BEFORE PR #147's
# packaging fix, so it still carried PROMPT_REVIEW_LEDGER.md (425 lines,
# a private citizen's name) + the test package + 38 unallowlisted prompts.
# PR #147 fixed the build; the stale artifact stayed tracked until now.
# Distributions are release assets, not source — build them fresh from a
# clean checkout at release time, never commit them.
*.whl
*.tar.gz
02_Core_Project/zspan_cli/build/
02_Core_Project/zspan_cli/dist/
# The vendored prompt copy setup.py generates at build time. The canonical
# prompts live in 02_Core_Project/prompts/; tracking this copy would let it
# drift from them and re-create the stale-vendored-artifact problem that
# once shipped an internal review ledger inside a wheel.
02_Core_Project/zspan_cli/zspan_cli/_prompts/

# Reference projects pulled in for inspection (kept on disk only)
03_Research/ganymede-backend/
03_Research/<private-predecessor-repo>/

# Worker subprocess log files (per-WO, regenerable, possibly large)
**/worker_logs/
# Haiku HTML scraper per-invocation audit-trail logs (S-036 V1)
agents/_haiku_html_scraper_logs/

# Throwaway experiment outputs (not committed)
experiments/

# HQ handoff: local snapshot of client/ source copied in for the
# Claude-design session. Kept on disk only — it's a transient handoff
# convenience, NOT canonical source. Committing it would duplicate the
# client/ tree into git and silently drift from the real source. The
# DESIGN_BRIEF.md + PROJECT_CONTEXT.md + README.md in that folder ARE
# committed; only the copied project_files/ snapshot is ignored.
01_Project_Overview/HANDOFF_ZSPAN_HQ/project_files/

# Claude Code session state (.claude/ everywhere, in full). Session
# tooling is workshop, never a public artifact — skills, couriers,
# prompt templates, handoffs, launch configs all stay local (D-154
# ADDENDUM 2026-07-07: ".claude/ in full — session tooling is
# workshop"). The pre-remake tree carried tracked-skills carve-outs
# here; repo v3 deliberately does not (2026-07-07 session-38 audit —
# a surviving carve-out structurally invites accidental workshop
# publication). The flagship's working copy keeps these dirs on disk;
# the governance-corpus backup stanza covers them off-machine.
.claude/*
**/.claude/*

# ── Operator-internal working docs — kept out of the published tree ────
# The public application tree excludes the internal operating manual,
# strategy corpus, task ledgers, and fleet
# docs are disk-only and never belong in it. All untracked today — these
# patterns are belt-and-suspenders so a stray `git add` from the repo root
# can't sweep one onto a branch bound for the public repo. Root-anchored so
# same-named files nested elsewhere are unaffected.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/AUTOPILOT_PROTOCOL.md
/ROADMAP.md
/TASKS.md
/TASKS_ARCHIVE.md
/BRAINSTORM_LOG.md
/HUMAN_API_HANDOFF.md
/OCTANE_MODE_EXPERIMENT.md
/respawn.md
/respawn-mac-migration-2026-06-14.md
/01_Project_Overview/
/agents/
/04_Operator_Side/

# ── Journals — operator's living voice-memo / brainstorm space ─────────
# Context-only sealed corpus (CLAUDE.md § journals). Disk-only like the
# verbatim ledger; guard against a stray root `git add` sweeping it toward
# a public-bound tree. (session-88 CF audit: journals/FABLE_AUDIT_*.md holds
# the operator email.)
/journals/

# ── Verbatim ledger — operator's exact words behind each decision ──────
# Local-only anti-"telephone-game" record (operator-directed 2026-07-18):
# James's verbatim messages that produced each decision, so a distilled
# D-entry can always be checked against what he actually said. NEVER
# published to GitHub — this is the raw operator voice, disk-only.
/verbatim_ledger/

# ── Research archive — intellectual lineage, disk-only by default ──────
# 03_Research/ is the local brainstorming and research archive. Keep it out
# of the application source tree so experiments and generated results are not
# mistaken for product code or public data.
/03_Research/*

# Per-run diagnostic + smoke JSON dumps in parsers/. Regenerable,
# per-machine, never load-bearing. Examples: mac_*_result.json (Mac
# claude-relay round-trip diagnostic outputs), _smoke_*.json /
# _smoke_*.py (one-shot smoke artifacts that landed in scripts/ during
# iteration). Added 2026-06-11 post-audit .gitignore triage.
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/mac_*_result.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/mac_*_diagnostic.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/scripts/_smoke_*

# Per-agent heartbeat transcripts + crashes.csv (per-run, large JSONL, regenerable).
# Each role's settings.json lives at agents/<role>.settings.json (committed);
# the dirs under ops/<role>-logs/ are the audit-trail outputs, not configuration.
ops/*-logs/

# D-099 Phase 2.1b — PC agent relay per-callback audit logs (regenerable,
# day-rotated JSONL). The relay scaffolding + STATUS.json IS committed;
# only the per-day audit log files are not.
02_Core_Project/pc_agent_relay/audit_logs/

# Mac node handshake/state files are LIVE self-written by each node on its
# heartbeat (host_lan_ip, base_url, timestamps) — they cannot be scrubbed in
# place (the node re-writes them next heartbeat) and post-D-111 loopback
# consolidation they're per-machine dormant handshake state. Untracked
# 2026-07-12 (audit / RR-1 SCRUB) so the public repo carries no operator LAN
# topology; the node scaffolding (server.py, SETUP.md) documents the
# architecture publicly without the machine detail.
02_Core_Project/mac_claude_relay/STATUS.json
02_Core_Project/mac_transcriber/STATUS.json
02_Core_Project/mac_diarizer/STATUS.json

# Per-agent runtime state files (the .gitkeep tracks the dir; the snapshot
# files are written by the agents' state-write wrappers and are per-machine).
agents/_custodian_state/parser-health.json
agents/_scout_state/*.json

# Bundled documentation exports for external AI ingestion (NotebookLM / Gemini)
docs_export_*/

# Ephemeral session scratch dir — used by Claude Code sessions for
# intermediate output (json/log files from background tasks, etc.).
# Untracked accumulation noise in `git status`; explicit ignore here.
.tmp/

# Quote-discipline preview sidecars (2026-06-23) — operator-side preview
# extractions for the V1-RAG-3 selection-discipline before/after toggle
# on BroadcastPage. Path served by /api/preview/quotes/:meeting_id.
.preview/

# ── Public parser source + private operational artifacts ──────────
# Active parser implementations are part of Z-SPAN's public source. Trial and
# superseded variants remain local until promoted to an active parser file.
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/*_parser_codex_trial*.py
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/*_parser_v*.py
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/parser_index.json
# Endpoint exports belong in the separate Civic Source Catalog.
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/data/Arizona_*.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/src/data/Arizona_*.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/CATALOG_CHECKLIST.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/_endpoint_catalog/

# Generated diagnostics, operator records, and research outputs are not
# application source.
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/PARSER_SUMMARY.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/coverage_index.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/health_report_*.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/financial_reports/
registry/registry_manifest.json
ops/registry_tools/seal_registry.py
ops/scan_built_artifacts_for_vendor_hosts.py
ops/migrate_to_fresh_repo.sh
02_Core_Project/zspan_cli/zspan_cli/tests/data/meeting_104003_discussion.json

# Librarian safeguard code is public. Its adversarial pass/fail corpus and
# tests that enumerate the exact rule matrix remain private.
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/input_security/librarian_gate_cases.v1.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/input_security/librarian_gate_cases.v2.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/input_security/librarian_stencil_cases.v1.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/input_security/librarian_stencil_cases.v2.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/input_security/test_librarian_input_gate.py
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/input_security/test_librarian_query_stencil.py
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/src/lib/librarianInputGate.test.ts
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/src/lib/librarianQueryStencil.test.ts

# client/public/ is a strict publication surface.
# It ships to every visitor as directly-addressable static assets, so no dev
# scripts, no in-progress crop comparisons, no operator screenshots, no
# NotebookLM (or successor) metadata files. Belt-and-suspenders — the scanner
# at ops/scan_public_tree_for_dev_artifacts.py fails the build on any such
# file; these .gitignore rules stop a stray `git add` from ever staging them.
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/**/*.py
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/**/*.meta.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/**/*.smoke.prompt.txt
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/hq/crops/
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/hq/composite_for_critique.png
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/client/public/hq/press_infographic.png
# Aggregated council roster stays operator-local under the D-153 sealed-corpus
# rationale (operator direction 2026-07-24).
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/council_members_data.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/city_intelligence/*.json
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/parsers/USER_SETTINGS_KEYS.md
# per-state discovery outputs (the "where") stay local; the framework
# README + schema in state_scaffolding/ are the public face:
02_Core_Project/council_navigator/state_scaffolding/*/

# Provider-agnostic emergency onboarding (S-146 / disk-only per D-154 —
# references the governance corpus; survives via the RED DRIVE root *.md loop)
/EMERGENCY_ONBOARDING.md

# The project genotype — INTERNAL RECOVERY MATERIAL (2026-07-14 tank). One
# self-contained blueprint that lets a fresh AI regrow a sibling of the project
# from zero artifacts. Governance-corpus member: carries internal doctrine +
# operator voice + active-prompt bodies, so it stays OFF the public repo (D-154)
# — survives via the RED DRIVE root *.md loop, plaintext by principle (an idea
# cannot be removed). The seal rides inside it: no recipes / secrets / endpoints.
/PROJECT_GENOTYPE.md

# Codex CLI project config + session artifacts — infrastructure config, untracked-by-design
# (same class as AGENTS.md per D-154; the /zspan-pr-check sensitivity sweep watches this family)
.codex/

# Prompt review queue — operator review surface, stays disk-side (James 2026-07-19).
# Holds unreviewed claude_authored prompt drafts + internal review reasoning.
02_Core_Project/prompts/PROMPT_REVIEW_LEDGER.md

# Project Room — the read-only collaboration projection (session-94 canvas
# think-tank). Projects governance-corpus content (TEMPORARY_THOUGHTS calls,
# railroad state), so the whole dir stays untracked-by-design like its
# sources. Durability rides the RED DRIVE backup, not git.
project_room/
